# Selection instructions
- Choose the single candidate probe that best fits the current point in the interview
- Consider which probe will elicit the most valuable new information given what has already been discussed
- Prefer probes that follow naturally from the interviewee's most recent response
- Avoid selecting a probe that revisits topics already covered in the transcript
- If the selected probe could be improved with minor rewording for naturalness, you may lightly rephrase it — but preserve its intent and probing strategy
- Reply only with the selected (or lightly rephrased) probe question, without any commentary or justification
